    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only concrete test class (the others are base/support classes). The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented rejection of a create-owner request whose lower-cased email duplicates an existing owner's, responding **409**, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (modeled on the existing telephone-uniqueness check).\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`EnsureEmailUnique.java`** (new function) \u2014 runs after `ValidateOwnerFields` has trimmed/lower-cased the email. It skips the check for an absent email (email is optional), and otherwise compares the request's lower-cased email against every existing owner's lower-cased email, throwing `DuplicateEmailException` on a match.\n\n2. **`DuplicateEmailException.java`** (new checked exception) \u2014 so it appears in the `throws` clause and routes to the escalation handler.\n\n3. **`DuplicateEmailExceptionHandler.java`** (new handler) \u2014 responds `409 CONFLICT` with `{\"errors\":[\"email\"]}`, matching the telephone handler's shape.\n\n4. **`...DuplicateEmailException.yml`** (new escalation wiring).\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `ensureUniqueEmail` step (with `govern: [ transaction ]`) into the pipeline right after `ensureUniqueTelephone`.\n\nThe full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`), including the new `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` acceptance test.",
